cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. No canonical citation format
  has been agreed for this project yet; the fields below are the facts
  confirmed locally (from pyproject.toml and this run's git history), not
  a fully worked-out citation record. hoh is the package, module, and CLI
  that implement the Harness-of-Harness pattern; VeriHarness is the project
  built on that pattern and the name this citation records.
title: "VeriHarness: an evidence-bound Harness-of-Harness for verifiable long-horizon agent development"
version: 0.4.0a2
date-released: "2026-10-21"
# date-released: the date of the documentation checkpoint at which the pre-release is
# cut; the operator may move it if the tag is cut on another day.
# Provenance: this file said `version: 0.1.0` with `date-released: "2026-09-08"`
# until 2026-10-07, when `version` became the pre-release; the date that
# belonged to 0.1.0 does not belong to 0.3.0a1 and is not carried over. It said
# `version: 0.3.0a1` with `date-released: "2026-10-07"` until 2026-10-09, when
# `version` became 0.3.0a2 (the a1 tag was cut on 2026-10-08, see RELEASE_NOTES.md).
# It said `version: 0.3.0a2` with `date-released: "2026-10-09"` until 2026-10-11, when
# `version` became 0.3.0a3 (the a2 tag was cut on 2026-10-09, see RELEASE_NOTES.md);
# the date is that of the documentation checkpoint and moves with the tag.
# It said `version: 0.3.0a3` with `date-released: "2026-10-11"` until 2026-10-13, when
# `version` became 0.3.0 (the a3 tag was cut on 2026-10-11, see RELEASE_NOTES.md); the date
# is that of the tag `v0.3.0`, the release at which phase P2 is closed (the closure record is
# the ledger entry O268; this is a release, not a pre-release, and readiness is not claimed).
authors:
  - given-names: "Furkan"
    family-names: "Sakızlı"
license: "MIT"
# See LICENSE at the repository root: the captain decided MIT for this
